      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand, we need to calculate the circumference of the circle it traces out. The second hand is 6 cm long, so its circumference is given by $2 \\pi r$, where $r$ is the length of the second hand. In this case, $r=6$, so the circumference is $2 \\pi (6) = 12 \\pi$ cm.\n\nSince the second hand completes one full revolution every minute, in 30 minutes it will complete 30 full revolutions. Therefore, the total distance traveled by the tip of the second hand is $30 \\times 12 \\pi = 360 \\pi$ cm. The final answer is $\\boxed{360 \\pi}$.The answer is: 360\\pi",
