      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a 30-minute period, we need to calculate the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand and then find out how much of this circumference is covered in 30 minutes.\n\n1. **Determine the Circumference of the Circle:**\n   The second hand moves in a circle with a radius of 6 cm. The formula for the circumference \\( C \\) of a circle is given by:\n   \\[\n   C = 2 \\pi r\n   \\]\n   where \\( r \\) is the radius. Substituting the given radius:\n   \\[\n   C = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Distance Traveled in 30 Minutes:**\n   Since the second hand completes one full revolution (circumference) in 60 minutes, it will complete \\( \\frac{30}{60} = \\frac{1}{2} \\) of a full revolution in 30 minutes. Therefore, the distance traveled in 30 minutes is half of the circumference:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 \\pi = 6 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the tip of the second hand travels \\(\\boxed{6\\pi}\\) centimeters during a 30-minute period.",
