    "text": "To determine how far the tip of the second hand travels during a period of 30 minutes, we need to calculate the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in one minute and then multiply that by 30.\n\nFirst, let's find the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand. The second hand is 6 cm long, so the radius of the circle is 6 cm. The formula for the circumference \\(C\\) of a circle is given by:\n\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi r\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the radius \\(r = 6\\) cm, we get:\n\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThis means that the tip of the second hand travels \\(12 \\pi\\) cm in one complete revolution around the circle. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, the tip of the second hand completes 60 revolutions in one hour. Therefore, in 30 minutes, the tip of the second hand completes half of these revolutions, which is 30 revolutions.\n\nTo find the total distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in 30 minutes, we multiply the circumference of the circle by the number of revolutions:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = 30 \\times 12 \\pi = 360 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThus, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{360\\pi}\n\\]",
